skill.resource _Edit_Protocol_ in usage.information = {
  The editing protocol for Term-addressed patches, previews, saved-result inspection and recovery, including Knowledge transfers, complete-Term Declaration Group edits and malformed-source repair.
.relations
  references _Source_Authoring_
  references _Corpus_Change_Procedure_
  references _Edit_Term_Declarations_
  references _Move_Terms_
.explanation
  - Use knowledge edit with Update Knowledge context hunks for header-only changes under _Source_Authoring_; retain complete-source replacement for intentional whole-Knowledge work. Knowledge identity changes use knowledge rename.
  - Use Add Term, Update Term and Delete Term blocks in one term edit patch for additions, changes and removals. Add requires an existing Knowledge destination; Delete refuses surviving references after the complete patch. Preview changes, and inspect saved results and partial failures. Knowledge transfer moves a Term with its single Term Declaration; Group edits address one complete Term Declaration. For malformed source, inspect diagnostic locations and the supported source repair path before resuming Term-addressed edits.
  - Reading context: _Corpus_Change_Procedure_, _Edit_Term_Declarations_, _Move_Terms_.
}


